---
description: Extract handlers into named functions; never inline async IIFEs in JSX.
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Named handlers

Do not put control flow in JSX props. Extract a named function in the component (or a hook).

```tsx
// BAD
<Button
  onClick={() => {
    void (async () => {
      setIsResending(true);
      try {
        await requestMagicLink(email);
      } finally {
        setIsResending(false);
      }
    })();
  }}
/>

// GOOD
const resend = async () => {
  setIsResending(true);
  try {
    await requestMagicLink(email);
  } finally {
    setIsResending(false);
  }
};

<Button onClick={() => void resend()} />
```

Same for `onSubmit`, `onChange`, and `form.handleSubmit(...)`. One-line wrappers like `() => void resend()` are fine. `try`/`finally`, awaits, and state updates are not.
